const a='/equipment/09-03/',u='https://download.tek.com/manual/2450-900-01E_Aug_2019_User.pdf',d='https://download.tek.com/manual/2450-901-01_D_May_2015_Ref.pdf',ds='https://www.tek.com/en/datasheet/smu-2400-graphical-sourcemeter/model-2450-touchscreen-source-measure-unit-smu-instrument',photo='https://www.tek.com/-/media/datasheets/category-cc-1-sources-and-supplies-2450.jpg';
const scopeAvailable=Object.keys(import.meta.glob('../09-04/simulator.astro')).length>0;
const refs=[['front','Operator panel',u+'#page=13','User manual 2450-900-01E, fig. 2 (p. 2-2). Compared display and encoder placement, key banks, four force/sense jacks, and earth terminal.'],['rear','Rear connections',u+'#page=13','Same revision, fig. 1 (p. 2-2). Compared four triax ports, AC inlet, interlock, vent fields and communications connectors. Rear bank is illustrative only.'],['side','Side & envelope',d+'#page=76','Reference manual 2450-901-01D, figs. 32–33 (pp. 2-49–2-50). Compared length, low front handle pivot, guards and short folded handle.'],['work','Working connection',u+'#page=45','User manual rev. E, fig. 22 (p. 5-4). HI mates to one resistor contact; LO to the other. Each contact gets a second, separate sense wire for Kelvin measurements. Generic coupon geometry is original.']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Keithley 2450 SourceMeter" subtitle="" description="Measure a resistive coupon with a live 3D SourceMeter, a current ceiling, and Kelvin leads." wide={true}>
<article id="smu" class="equipment smu">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-03/">← Equipment 09-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#smu-references">References</a><a href="#smu-verify">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="head"><p class="eq-meta">09-03 / Electrical characterization / Instrument bench</p><h2>Keithley 2450 SourceMeter</h2><p>Watch a current limit take over from a voltage source. A generic 1 kΩ coupon is already connected to the front banana jacks of the standard benchtop 2450. Run the sweep once; then change the current limit from 2 to 0.5 mA and compare the last reading.</p></header>
<div class="bench">
<section class="card"><h3>01 · Inspect the bench</h3><div class="bar" id="views">{['Bench','Front','Rear','Side','Work'].map(s=><button type="button" data-view={s.toLowerCase()}>{s}</button>)}<button id="xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="instrument" aria-label="Orbitable SourceMeter instrument and resistor coupon"></canvas><p class="small" id="loadstate" aria-live="polite">Loading 3D instrument…</p>
<p class="small">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom; Bench resets the view. Select a force or sense jack to reconnect its lead pair, the encoder to cycle the limit, or the ON/OFF key to run. All actions also have panel controls. The depicted front/rear selector stays on FRONT.</p>
</section>
<section class="card"><h3>02 · Configure and measure</h3><form id="cfg"><div class="fields">
<label>Specimen ID<input name="sampleId" value="coupon-1k-01" maxlength="96" required /></label>
<label>Source mode<select name="mode"><option value="V">Source V / limit I</option><option value="I">Source I / limit V</option></select></label>
<label>DUT resistance (Ω)<input name="rOhm" type="number" value="1000" min="1" max="1000000" step="any" required /></label>
<label>Per force lead (Ω)<input name="leadOhm" type="number" value="0" min="0" max="100" step="any" required /></label>
<label>Sensing<select name="sense"><option value="2">Local · two wire</option><option value="4">Remote · four wire</option></select></label>
<label>Compliance <span data-unit="limit">(mA)</span><input name="limit" type="number" value="2" step="any" required /></label>
<label>Start <span data-unit="request">(V)</span><input name="start" type="number" value="0" step="any" required /></label>
<label>Stop <span data-unit="request">(V)</span><input name="stop" type="number" value="1" step="any" required /></label>
<label>Points<input type="number" name="n" min="2" max="201" value="11" required /></label>
<label>Dwell (s)<input type="number" name="dwellS" min=".001" max="10" step="any" value=".1" required /></label>
<label>Continuity threshold (Ω)<input name="continuityOhm" type="number" min=".1" max="1000000" step="any" value="50" required /></label>
<label>Readout noise<select name="noise"><option value="false">Off</option><option value="true">Synthetic · seeded</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button type="button" id="fixture">Disconnect DUT</button><button type="button" id="senseLeads">Disconnect sense pair</button><button type="button" id="cycleLimit">Cycle limit</button><button type="button" id="demo">Restore example</button></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="run" type="submit" id="run">Run sweep</button><button type="button" id="off">Output off</button></div></form>
<p id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Output off. Ready to run.</p></section>
</div>
<section class="card readings"><h3>03 · Read the coupon</h3><div class="bar" id="exports"><button data-export="json" disabled>Result JSON</button><button data-export="csv" disabled>Point CSV</button><button data-export="wave" disabled>Voltage waveform JSON</button></div>
<p id="summary" aria-live="polite">No acquisition yet.</p><svg id="chart" viewBox="0 0 740 220" role="img" aria-label="Simulated DUT voltage vs time; dots indicate current or voltage compliance"></svg>
<details><summary>Individual readings and compliance flags</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>{['t (s)','Request','Measured V','Measured mA','DUT V','Terminal V','Limited'].map(h=><th>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div></details></section>
<section id="smu-references"><h3>Instrument file &amp; illustrated references</h3><p>The selected configuration is the standard front-panel model 2450 with its benchtop bumpers and folded carry handle, not the NFP or rack variant. No specimen is inserted into the chassis. <a href={photo}>Manufacturer front-panel photograph</a>: screen proportions, rotary control and terminal colors. Original geometry renders below are paired with the manufacturer’s illustrations; they are not photographs or factory CAD.</p>
<div class="refs">{refs.map(([view,title,url,desc])=><figure><img src={a+view+'.webp'} loading="lazy" width="720" height="440" alt={'Original reconstruction: '+title}/><figcaption><strong>{title}.</strong> {desc} <a href={url}>Compare original</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value / conditions</th><th>Use &amp; source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Bench envelope W × H × D</td><td>255.3 × 106.1 × 425.4 mm, handle folded</td><td>Geometric datums. <a href={d+'#page=75'}>Rev D, figs. 32–33, pp. 2-49–50</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Bare chassis envelope</td><td>213 × 88 × 403 mm without bumpers or handle</td><td>Cross-check, rounded. <a href={ds}>Datasheet / General</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Front panel</td><td>5-inch touch display, four banana measurement terminals</td><td>Operator layout. <a href={u+'#page=13'}>Rev E, fig. 2</a> and <a href={ds}>datasheet</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rated output</td><td>20 W, four quadrants; up to ±21 V at 1 A range or ±210 V at 100 mA range</td><td>Hardware envelope, not simultaneous maxima. <a href={ds}>Operating characteristics</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Remote sense</td><td>≤5 V force-to-sense drop; input impedance &gt;10 GΩ</td><td>Hardware bound; modeled lead drop ≤1 V per lead; ideal infinite sense impedance. <a href={ds}>Remote sensing</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Experiment range</td><td>±10 V / ±10 mA, 1 Ω–1 MΩ DUT, 0–100 Ω per lead, 2–201 points, 1 ms–10 s dwell</td><td>Original software bounds, resistive DC only; not the 2450’s resolution or full range.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>What the instrument calculates</h3><p>Current is positive from FORCE HI to LO, and voltage is HI minus LO. For DUT resistance R and per-lead resistance r, the feedback resistance is R + 2r for local sensing and R for four-wire sensing. In voltage mode, I = clamp(V<sub>set</sub>/R<sub>feedback</sub>, ±I<sub>limit</sub>). In current mode, I = clamp(I<sub>set</sub>, ±V<sub>limit</sub>/R<sub>feedback</sub>). DUT voltage is IR; force-terminal voltage is I(R + 2r). Compliance means the requested point exceeded the ideal limit, not merely that it equaled it.</p>
<p>Remote leads sense at the coupon with zero modeled sense current. Optional deterministic Gaussian readout noise (1 µV and 1 nA RMS) is synthetic, not tied to an instrument range or NPLC. Apparent resistance uses measured V/I at the largest absolute current; the continuity flag compares it to your threshold. A zero-current sweep gives no resistance verdict. Invalid loads or missing required connections produce no result.</p>
<p>Each sweep assigns times starting at zero and spaced by the selected dwell, not wall clock time. Export JSON for ideal and simulated readings, units, contact IDs, source settings and parent/result revisions; CSV for data analysis; waveform JSON for compatible voltage-trace consumers. The revision tracks a measurement, not a physical change to the resistor. <a href={a+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a> · <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a> · <a href={a+'example-waveform.json'}>Waveform example</a>.</p></section>
{scopeAvailable && <p><a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/?from=09-03">Open the 1 kΩ example on the 09-04 oscilloscope →</a> To inspect your own run instead, export Voltage waveform JSON above and import it at the scope. The eleven original readings span 1 s at 10 samples/s. Connecting dots does not model analog slew.</p>}
<section id="smu-verify"><h3>Verification notebook</h3><p>Expected values were declared before implementation. These are analytic checks, not validation against measurements from a real unit. Actual results use SI units (V, A). Missing-circuit tests check that no points are produced.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>{verified.map(v=><tr><td>{v.id}</td><td>{v.expected}</td><td>{v.actual}</td><td>{v.tolerance}</td><td>{v.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}{geom.checks.map(v=><tr><td>Geometry · {v.axis}</td><td>{v.referenceMm} mm</td><td>{v.actualMm} mm</td><td>±{v.toleranceMm} mm</td><td>{v.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p>Exterior dimensions exclude removable leads and the original coupon. Panel features, cable paths and folded handle profile are estimated from the linked images. Rear jacks and communication ports are not live. This simulator does not predict timing transients, thermal behavior, contact nonlinearity, leakage floors or instrument uncertainty.</p></section>
<section><h3>3D &amp; integration files</h3><p><a href={a+'keithley-2450.glb'} download>True-scale GLB</a> · <a href={a+'model.py'}>Editable Blender generator</a> + <a href={a+'pack.py'}>mesh packer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Interaction anchors</a> · <a href={a+'solver.mjs'}>Headless solver/actions</a> · <a href={a+'reference-cases.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Numerical results</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-check.json'}>Geometry checks</a>.</p>
<p>The asset uses meters, {metrics.triangles.toLocaleString('en-US')} triangles, {metrics.drawCalls} material primitives and {(metrics.bytes/1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB. Movable/operable parts have stable node IDs and hit bounds. WebXR, when available, places the instrument at bench height and uses controller selection for leads, limit and output. Desktop and touch controls do not need a headset; physical Quest 3 performance and interaction are unverified.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
